As per my research, the bug is generated after commit https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/commit/bba74985ab57c16501058fff93ff657a1af2efb6 
Maybe @thdxr made these regarding the new v2 opencode changes.  
@Edison-A-N  can you please verify it once

It's due to the fact that the fff system gets mounted to /home dir, which causes this issue 
`OPENCODE_DISABLE_FFF=1 npm run dev -- serve --port 4096` This can fix it temporarily.

```/home/jashan
{
  ok: false,
  error: "Failed to init file picker: Can not run certain FFF features in a file system root or home directories. Consider smaller per-project directories.",
}```

@StarpTech if this isn't the place to post this, feel free to direct me elsewhere and/or delete this comment.

That said, I've had a long standing desire to see a particular use case supported by the plugin ecosystem, which is proper orchestration (HITL, agent routing, etc) controls via the plugin API. If you're still looking for concrete use cases, I would be glad to detail out some of my thoughts around the plugin I've envisioned, the current shortfalls of v1, and what primitives/hooks would be needed to fully support proper orchestration via plugins.

Also, it's worth noting that the plugin I envisioned is slightly broader in scope than just request hooks, but I think this is the core area where it might be relevant. If that sounds at all relevant, let me know and we I'd be delighted to discuss it further.
